course: dictionary
lesson: 8166
title: A formal word: reside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Reside» is a formal word that means live. You will meet it on official letters, on forms and in stories about kings. «The court hereby orders that the child shall reside with the applicant.» Lexi asks what it means: a judge is saying where the child must live.
explain: Use the context clues. The court is making an official order about a child's home, so the word that fits is live. Check by swapping: «shall live with the applicant» still makes sense, so reside means live.
explain: Reside has a second meaning: to be found in or belong to something. «Power resides with the people» means the power belongs to the people. In science, «the information resides in the cell's nucleus» means it is kept inside the nucleus.
explain: Watch the family of words. A resident is a person who lives in a place, and a residence is a home. So a letter about someone's residence is about their house, and a resident of a town is someone who lives there.
fact: Reside is a verb, so its forms are resides, resided and residing.
fact: «Reside» means to live in a place, as in «She resides in Toronto.»
fact: «Reside» can also mean to be found in or belong to something, as in «Power resides with the people.»
fact: A resident is a person who lives in a place, and a residence is a home.
fact: «Reside» is a formal word, so you will mostly see it in official letters, forms and stories. In everyday talk, live is the usual word.
exercise: «She resides in Toronto.» What does resides mean here? | Works in a shop | Visits | Leaves | *Lives
exercise: «Power resides with the people.» What does resides mean here? | Is hidden under the floor | Runs away from | Is broken into pieces | *Belongs to, or is found in
exercise: Which word means a person who lives in a place? | *resident | president | rescue | residue
test: «The court orders that the child shall reside with the applicant.» In this sentence, reside means | *Live | Play | Hide | Study
test: Which word names a home? | resident | reside | *residence | residue
exam: «The information resides in the cell's nucleus.» Lexi asks what resides means here. | Is cut into pieces | *Is kept inside, or is found in | Is shown on a screen | Is moved outside
